**Summary**

- **Primary request & intent**  
  - You wanted to continue the coding session after a previous interruption, focusing on the status‑bar UI implementation.

- **Key technical concepts**  
  - **Status‑bar rendering** – a flex container with three logical groups:  
    1. **Model selector** (left) – left‑aligned badge.  
    2. **Thinking level selector** (center) – right‑aligned badge.  
    3. **Context usage** (right) – a popover that shows context‑usage percentage, warning, and action buttons (Compact / New).  
  - **Responsive layout** – uses a grid with `grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;` so the left/right groups stay separate on narrow sidebars.  
  - **Responsive breakpoints** – `@container (max-width: 300px)` hides debug tokens and limits the width of the context pill.  
  - **Accessibility** – `aria-label`s on buttons, focus‑visible outlines, and tooltip positioning.  
  - **Interaction** – click handlers dispatch custom events (`pi:status-update`, `pi:command-run`) to update the UI and model selector.  
  - **Styling** – Tailwind‑like utility classes (`bg-alpha-2`, `border`, `font-sans`, `--text-sm`, etc.) with responsive `@container` rules.

- **Files and code sections**  
  - **Files read / edited**  
    - `src/taskpane/status-bar.ts` – updated to use `pi-status-tooltip--right` class for the mode badge, align left/right badges, and add responsive `@container` rules.  
    - `src/ui/theme/components/status-bar.css` – changed `max-width` to `min(200px, calc(100vw - 24px))` for the context pill, and added `@container` media queries to shrink the context pill on narrow viewports.  
    - `src/ui/theme/components/status-bar.css` – added `@container (max-width: 260px)` to hide the debug token on very narrow viewports.  
    - `src/ui/theme/components/status-bar.css` – moved `display: flex` to a `.pi-status-main` class to separate left/right groups.  
  - **Key code snippets** (excerpted from the final commit):
    ```css
    .pi-status-bar {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
      align-items: start;
      column-gap: 6px;
      row-gap: 4px;
      padding: 4px;
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: var(--text-sm);
      letter-spacing: 0.01em;
      color: var(--muted-foreground);
      overflow: visible;
      min-width: 0;
      position: relative;
      z-index: 20;
      container-type: inline-size;
    }
    .pi-status-main {
      min-width: 0;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 6px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .pi-status-side {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: flex-end;
    }
    .pi-status-model {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 4px;
      background: var(--alpha-2);
      border: 1px solid transparent;
      cursor: pointer;
      padding: 2px 6px;
      margin: -2px 0;
      border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: var(--text-sm);
      color: var(--foreground);
      opacity: 0.78;
      transition: background var(--duration-fast), color var(--duration-fast), opacity var(--duration-fast), border-color var(--duration-fast);
      min-width: 0;
      overflow: visible;
    }
    .pi-status-model:hover {
      background: var(--pi-green-lighter);
      border-color: var(--green-alpha-20);
      color: var(--foreground);
    }
    .pi-status-model__mark {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: var(--text-base);
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--primary);
      line-height: 1;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }
    .pi-status-model__name {
      white-space: nowrap;
      overflow: hidden;
      text-overflow: ellipsis;
      min-width: 0;
    }
    .pi-status-model svg {
      flex-shrink: 0;
      opacity: 0.6;
    }
    .pi-status-model svg,
    .pi-status-model svg * {
      pointer-events: none;
    }
    /* … other styles … */
    .pi-status-mode {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 3px;
      border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
      padding: 2px 6px;
      font-size: var(--text-xs);
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      line-height: 1.4;
      cursor: pointer;
      white-space: nowrap;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      transition: background var(--duration-fast), border-color var(--duration-fast), color var(--duration-fast);
    }
    .pi-status-mode--auto {
      border: 1px solid oklch(0.66 0.19 145 / 0.38);
      background: oklch(0.66 0.19 145 / 0.12);
      color: oklch(0.45 0.15 145);
    }
    .pi-status-mode--auto:hover {
      background: oklch(0.66 0.19 145 / 0.2);
      border-color: oklch(0.66 0.19 145 / 0.48);
    }
    .pi-status-mode--confirm {
      border: 1px solid oklch(0.65 0.17 40 / 0.38);
      background: oklch(0.65 0.17 40 / 0.12);
      color: oklch(0.48 0.12 40);
    }
    .pi-status-mode--confirm:hover {
      background: oklch(0.65 0.17 40 / 0.2);
      border-color: oklch(0.65 0.17 40 / 0.48);
    }
    /* Context usage – left side (debug hidden on narrow view) */
    .pi-status-ctx {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 4px;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      white-space: nowrap;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      transition: color var(--duration-normal) ease;
      border: none;
      color: inherit;
    }
    .pi-status-ctx--trigger {
      border: 1px solid transparent;
      border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
      background: var(--alpha-3);
      padding: 2px 5px;
      margin: -2px 0;
      transition: background var(--duration-fast) ease, border-color var(--duration-fast) ease;
    }
    .pi-status-ctx--trigger:hover {
      background: var(--pi-green-lighter);
      border-color: var(--green-alpha-20);
    }
    .pi-status-ctx--yellow {
      color: var(--pi-yellow, #e5a100);
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    .pi-status-ctx--red {
      color: var(--destructive, #e5484d);
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    .pi-status-ctx__pct,
    .pi-status-ctx__sep,
    .pi-status-ctx__limit {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
    }
    .pi-status-ctx__sep {
      margin: 0 1px;
      opacity: 0.75;
    }
    /* Debug token – hidden on narrow view */
    .pi-status-ctx__debug {
      display: none;
    }
    @container (max-width: 260px) {
      .pi-status-ctx__sep,
      .pi-status-ctx__limit {
        display: none;
    }
    ```
  - **Conflict resolution** – the autostash was applied, but the final `git rebase --continue` succeeded because the changes were already present in `main`.

- **Errors and fixes**  
  - **Error when starting dev server** – Port 3000 was already in use by an existing `vite` process.  
    - **Fix:** Killed the existing process (`kill 22911`), started a new dev server (`npm run dev`), and verified the new process (`lsof -nP -iTCP:3000`).  
  - **No other errors** were reported during the session.

- **Problem solving**  
  - **Identified the visual inconsistency** (mode badge too small on narrow view).  
  - **Implemented responsive layout** using Tailwind‑style `@container` rules and `display: flex` for the left/right groups.  
  - **Added accessibility improvements** (aria‑labels, focus outlines).  
  - **Ensured tooltip alignment** on both sides of the status bar.

- **All user messages**  
  - The session contained a single user message summarizing the request and intent.

- **Pending tasks**  
  - None – the session is now complete and the code is merged into `main`.

- **Current work**  
  - The latest commit (`df6da77`) contains the fix for the status‑bar layout.  
  - No further actions are required at this time.

- **Next step**  
  - No further action required; the session can be closed.
